 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "When the oxygen masks drop, the most dangerous thing on the plane is how good you feel.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 112
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "barry",
   "text": "I feel fantastic!",
   "from": 120,
   "to": 158
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Barry is at thirty-five thousand feet, and he's in trouble.",
   "from": 166,
   "to": 234
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Out there, the air is so thin it can't keep a brain running.",
   "from": 242,
   "to": 329
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So the jet pumps air in and squeezes the cabin to feel like eight thousand feet.",
   "from": 336,
   "to": 429
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then a door seal cracks. Air screams out, the cabin fogs, and the needle climbs.",
   "from": 437,
   "to": 566
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Before it hits fifteen thousand, the ceiling pops open and the masks drop.",
   "from": 574,
   "to": 670
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Grandma Rose helps everyone else first. Barry pokes the flat bag and laughs.",
   "from": 680,
   "to": 791
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Nobody screams. And that should scare you.",
   "from": 798,
   "to": 886
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, a starving brain doesn't feel fear. It feels a warm, happy buzz.",
   "from": 902,
   "to": 1081
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Up here, that buzz gives you a minute at most to act.",
   "from": 1087,
   "to": 1164
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "sofia",
   "text": "Pull the mask down, breathe, then help!",
   "from": 1170,
   "to": 1238
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "That yank fires an oxygen generator: at least twelve minutes, even with a flat bag.",
   "from": 1244,
   "to": 1366
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The pilots mask up first, then dive to ten thousand feet, where air works again.",
   "from": 1373,
   "to": 1472
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So Barry stops giggling, and the whole plane wakes up.",
   "from": 1478,
   "to": 1541
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Up there, feeling great is the warning. Mask first, then help.",
   "from": 1549,
   "to": 1672
  }
 ],
